  <static seed="207" source="Contrib/DMOI/2-Sequences/2_3-Polynomial_Fitting/2_3_8.pg">
    <statement><p>Suppose 
Suppose <m>a_n = {3n^{2}-3n-5}\text{.}</m> Find a closed formula for the sequence of differences by computing <m>a_n - a_{n-1}\text{.}</m>  Simplify your answer as much as posible.</p>
<p><m>a_n - a_{n-1} =</m> <fillin characters="12" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>6n-6</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p><m>a_{n-1} = (n-1)^2  - 3(n-1)  - 5 = {3n^{2}-9n+1}</m>. Thus <m>a_n - a_{n-1} = {6n-6}\text{.}</m> 
Note that this is linear (arithmetic).</p>
</solution>
